## Revision delta from approved revision 5

The approved read-only feasibility check succeeded: GDB 15.1 attached without elevation to a disposable same-UID multithreaded Python process, produced four readable thread backtraces with 86 frame lines, and detached cleanly. One main-thread unwind warning and unavailable ptrace sysctl files are recorded. The probe did not attach to FFmpeg or capture camera data, and it establishes no SideCamera callsite or cadence cause.

Revision 6 proposes a separately scoped one-run GDB sampling diagnostic for BUILD. The saved futex association remains temporal same-address correlation, not waiter identity or causal proof. AC-4 still fails on the accepted five-minute run. No product source or production argv change is proposed.

## Finding and bounded BUILD path

The accepted five-minute current-source reproduction remains 6,050 matched frames over 302.506666 seconds, mean 20.000523 fps, maximum EOF gap 89.163715 ms, and 753/6,049 gaps above 60 ms. This fails AC-4's maximum-gap criterion. The known jitter remains localized after V4L2 dequeue and before raw-pipe delivery inside FFmpeg processing/output; the exact internal wait/processing cause is unresolved. PTS are V4L2 SOE, not EOF; keep `timestampEof` as host-monotonic time sampled after each complete raw-frame read.

**Owner:** BUILD through `build/build-management`; this revision-6 handoff is approved for the bounded diagnostic below.

Run one 600-frame diagnostic on the same assigned camera using the fixed FFmpeg executable and unchanged default production argv. Keep the 1280×720 MJPEG-to-NV12 mode, one decoder thread, one filter thread, queue size 1, same camera, and same reader. Save no frame payload. After startup, arm a one-shot monotonic watchdog for each in-flight full-frame read; if it remains incomplete for more than 60 ms, take at most one GDB snapshot for that read. Re-arm only after that frame completes; allow at most three snapshots total. Verify the target PID is the live FFmpeg child and `/proc/<pid>/exe` plus its command line match the fixed executable and expected argv. Use `gdb --quiet --batch --nx --pid <pid>` with pagination and confirmation off, debuginfod disabled, `info threads`, `thread apply all bt 16`, then detach and quit. Record monotonic trigger, attach, detach, and full-read-completion times, debugger pause duration, and TID/LWP mapping. Do not use `strace` or another tracer. Abort and clean up if PID verification, attach, backtrace collection, or detach fails.

GDB stops FFmpeg threads while collecting each snapshot, so these pauses perturb cadence and may extend each triggering gap. The snapshots are for callsite localization only; their timings cannot measure AC-4 and do not establish causality. This step is diagnostic only, makes no source or argv change, and does not replace a separate accepted five-minute AC-4 run.

